;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; jak-hd-physics.gc — Grecharged-secondary-motion: verlet/spring secondary-motion chains on the
;; HD companion skeletons (jiggle, hair, beards, straps, dangling accessories).
;;
;; PRINCIPLE (spring-toward-the-animated-target). fill-jak-hd-bones! (jak-hd.gc) overwrites every
;; HD joint's WORLD matrix each frame from the driver's animation. This pass runs IMMEDIATELY AFTER
;; that fill inside the same do-joint-math!: for each configured chain joint the freshly retargeted
;; matrix is the TARGET (the authored rest pose of this frame); the sim carries a verlet point per
;; joint (pos + prev) integrated with a spring toward the target plus gravity, then constraint
;; iterations (distance to parent from the LIVE target lengths — correct under any rig scale —,
;; swing-cone limit around the target direction, body collisions), then writes the joint matrix back
;; as: 3x3 rows post-multiplied by the minimal swing rotation (target-dir -> sim-dir; row lengths
;; preserved, so non-unit rig scales like Keira's 0.103 straps survive) and translation row =
;; simulated position. With zero excitation the spring converges to the target exactly -> subtle by
;; construction; physics OFF = pass skipped = bit-exact stock-HD.
;;
;; ================================ CYCLE 2 (owner verdict 16:40 + 17:35) =========================
;; (A) FAKE WIND vs PHYSICS — jak1 ALREADY animates straps / hair / cloth with authored pseudo-wind
;;     channels. Springing toward that target left TWO writers on the same bone: double motion, and
;;     Jak's blue cloth clipping. FIX = per-chain `anim` mode. `replace` (the default) RE-GLUES the
;;     chain to its BIND-POSE local transforms carried by the animated anchor BEFORE the targets are
;;     cached — i.e. the authored channel delta on a physics-owned joint is discarded and the sim is
;;     the only source of secondary motion. `excite` re-glues too but feeds the discarded authored
;;     delta back in as an input FORCE (never a second write). `keep` = the old behaviour.
;;     The re-glue is exactly fill-jak-hd-bones!'s mode-2 GLUE product, W'_k = L'_k . W'_par with
;;     L'_k = inv(bind-pose[k]) . bind-pose[par] (bind-pose slots STORE the inverse bind).
;; (B) HAIR ANCHORING — "the whole hair moves, as if detached from the skull". The chain ROOT was a
;;     free sim link. FIX = `rootlock=N`: the first N links ride the animated bone RIGIDLY (no
;;     integration, no constraint, NO write-back — the re-glued rest matrix stands), plus
;;     `gradient=G`, a root->tip freedom ramp that makes the first free links stiffer with a tighter
;;     swing cone and leaves the full amplitude to the tips.
;; (C) CHEST — see the params file: the cone/stretch limits were clipping the bounce.
;; (D) ACCESSORIES — goggles &co are chains like any other; class is a COST tier, not a hierarchy.
;; (17:35) COLLIDERS — a real body volume, not 1-2 symbolic spheres: `capsule A B radius=R` swept
;;     volumes following two animated bones, per-chain filters, `tier=` so a lower precision level
;;     thins the set without ever letting a chain pass visibly through the body, contact FRICTION
;;     (the push-out impulse is absorbed into `prev`, killing contact jitter) and a RESIDUAL
;;     PENETRATION counter measured after the last iteration — the owner's bar is resid=0.
;;
;; ================================ CYCLE 3 (owner verdict 2026-08-06 07:40) =====================
;; (A) AUTHORED ANIMATION HAS PRIORITY. ND sometimes DRIVES a secondary bone on purpose — Jak's
;;     ears reacting, Keira GRABBING her goggles and pulling them over her eyes. That is authored
;;     intent, not fake physics, and `anim=replace` was throwing it away. Fix = per chain
;;     `authored=T`: each frame the re-glue already knows the authored world offset it is about to
;;     discard; expressed as a fraction of the chain's own length that IS the "is the animator
;;     driving this?" signal. Above T (hysteresis at T/2) a blend weight w ramps to 1 at
;;     `authrise=` per second: the TARGET becomes the authored pose, stiffness is multiplied by
;;     `authstiff=`, gravity and excitation fade out and the chain stops colliding (the animator's
;;     pose wins, exactly as owner-specified). When the authored motion stops, w ramps back down at
;;     `authfall=` per second and physics RESUMES PROGRESSIVELY from where it is — the target slides
;;     back to the calm rest pose, so there is no snap by construction. Counters: engage/release
;;     events, held chain-frames, max blend.
;; (B) SPAWN AND BIG TRANSITIONS. Chains "went wild" at spawn and on hard pose cuts. Per chain the
;;     anchor's one-frame travel is watched: past max(PHYS-JUMP-ABS, 1.5x chain length) it is a
;;     teleport/cut, not motion, so the chain hard-resets to the authored rest AND takes a
;;     PHYS-SETTLE-frame ramp during which gravity, excitation and the visible deviation are scaled
;;     in from zero. A chain's first simulated frame goes down the same path, so every actor spawns
;;     at its bind pose with zero inherited velocity. `burst=` counts settle frames whose visible
;;     deviation still exceeded PHYS-BURST-REL of the chain length — owner bar: 0.
;; (C) TAPERED COLLIDERS. Constant-radius capsules cannot model Jak's FLARED trouser legs or his
;;     shoulders, so the jacket hem clipped through anyway. `radius2=` gives a capsule a second
;;     radius at its far end and the contact radius is interpolated at the contact point's own
;;     segment parameter — a cone, not a cylinder.
;; (D) THE FREEDOM RAMP MUST FIT THE CHAIN'S LENGTH. Jak's hair is TWO joints with rootlock=1, so
;;     exactly one link could ever move ("only the very tip of the tip"), and Keira's short back
;;     hair had the same shape. The ramp now has a configurable FLOOR (`rootfree=`) so the stiffest
;;     free link keeps a usable fraction of the cone instead of 1/nfree, and the short chains drop
;;     the rigid rootlock for a steep gradient — the root still visibly rides the skull, but the
;;     whole strand bends. Proof: per-LINK window spans (`jdev:`), so "the root is frozen" is a
;;     number, and `frozen=` counts ACTIVE chains that never moved in a window where the actor did.
;; (F) KEIRA'S SHOULDER STRAPS are REVERTED (see physics_chains.txt) — they were a regression.
;; DATA-DRIVEN: chains + params + precision levels live in recharged_assets/physics_chains.txt,
;; parsed C++-side (kmachine.cpp, OG_FEAT_PHYSICS) and queried over the pc-physics-* FFI at
;; companion init (joint NAMES resolved against the live HD jgeo). All FFI numeric returns are
;; MILLI-units (x1000) to avoid the float-return-register trap.
;;
;; SAFETY INVARIANT: after each chain step, any non-finite component or deviation > 2x chain
;; length hard-resets the chain state to the targets (+ nan-resets counter, must stay 0 in proofs).
;; An explosion can never persist more than one frame.
;;
;; PRECISION LADDER (owner-mandated monotone cost<->quality): per-level levers (substeps or fixed
;; 240Hz accumulator, constraint iterations, collider TIER, active chain-class mask) are DATA in the
;; [levels] section, selected by (-> *pc-settings* physics-quality) via pc-physics-enabled.
;;
;; PROOFS: [HD-PHYS] windowed counters (state dump: max deviation / max velocity bounded,
;; nan-resets, rest convergence when calm, rootdev=0 for locked roots, resid=0 penetrations,
;; per-chain deviation list so an INERT chain is visible as a number) — code-level evidence, never
;; capture campaigns.

(#when FLAG_PHYSICS

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; C++ FFI (kmachine.cpp, OG_FEAT_PHYSICS). All value returns are MILLI-units unless noted.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(define-extern pc-physics-reload (function int))
(define-extern pc-physics-enabled (function int))              ;; 0 = off, else level+1
(define-extern pc-physics-joint-role (function string string int))   ;; (chain<<8)|link, -1 none
(define-extern pc-physics-num-chains (function string int))
;; ids: 0 hz 1 damp 2 grav 3 maxangle-deg 4 inertia 5 stretch 6 radius
;;      7 rootlock 8 gradient 9 animmode 10 excite 11 friction
;;      12 authored 13 authrise 14 authfall 15 authstiff 16 rootfree 17 nodesc   (cycle 3)
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-param-mi (function string int int int))
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-flags (function string int int))    ;; class bits 1/2/4
(define-extern pc-physics-level-param-mi (function int int int))    ;; 0 substeps 1 iters 2 collide-tier 3 classmask 4 fixedhz
(define-extern pc-physics-joint-collider-mi (function string string int)) ;; milli radius, 0 none
(define-extern pc-physics-num-colliders (function string int))
;; 0 milli radius, 1 RAW chain mask (-1 = all), 2 RAW tier, 3 RAW 1 = capsule,
;; 4 milli FAR-END radius (tapered capsule; = field 0 when radius2= is absent)
(define-extern pc-physics-collider-param-mi (function string int int int))
(define-extern pc-physics-collider-is-joint (function string int string int)) ;; 1 if collider i sits on that joint
(define-extern pc-physics-collider-is-joint2 (function string int string int)) ;; 1 if capsule i ENDS on that joint
(define-extern pc-physics-generation (function int))    ;; bumped on every params (re)parse

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; static pools: 24 slots x 48 sim joints x 24 chains x 16 colliders.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(defconstant PHYS-SLOTS 24)
(defconstant PHYS-COMP-SLOTS 8)  ;; slots 0..7 are claimed by HD companions (bottom-up);
                                 ;; 8..23 by stock-model riders (top-down). One pool, no starvation
                                 ;; of the companions by a crowded village.
(defconstant PHYS-MAXJ 128)      ;; per-slot parent-table / descendant-pass joint ceiling
(defconstant PHYS-JPS 48)      ;; joints per slot
(defconstant PHYS-CPS 24)      ;; chains per slot
(defconstant PHYS-COLS 16)     ;; colliders per slot (cycle 2: a real body volume needs >8)

(define *phys-slot-pid* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-njoints* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-nchains* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-ncols* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-seeded* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-frames* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; window frame counter
(define *phys-slot-resets* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; nan/explosion resets (window)
(define *phys-slot-maxdev* (new 'static 'array float 24))    ;; window max |p - t|
(define *phys-slot-maxvel* (new 'static 'array float 24))    ;; window max per-frame speed
(define *phys-slot-calm* (new 'static 'array int32 24))      ;; consecutive calm frames
(define *phys-slot-anchprev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 24)) ;; chain0 anchor last pos (debug)
(define *phys-slot-anchmove* (new 'static 'array float 24))  ;; window max anchor move (debug)
;; ONE-LINE window emitter buffer: `format 0` is one logcat line per call on Android, so the whole
;; window must be assembled here and printed once (see the emitter at the bottom of this file).
;; Cycle 2 widened it: the per-chain deviation list rides in the SAME line (24 chains x ~13 chars).
;; Cycle 3 widened it again and added a SECOND line ([HD-PHYS2]: per-chain push-outs and the
;; per-LINK spans). The buffer is reused for both — appending to a string never splits a line, only
;; `format 0` does — so it must hold the LONGER of the two: 24 chains x ~11 + 48 links x ~15 + a
;; header. 2048 leaves better than 2x headroom over the worst case a full slot can produce.
(define *phys-line-buf* (new 'global 'string 2048 (the-as string #f)))
(define *phys-slot-pushouts* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; collision push-out events (window)
(define *phys-slot-maxpen* (new 'static 'array float 24))    ;; max penetration depth resolved (window)
;; ---- cycle-2 counters -------------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-slot-resid* (new 'static 'array int32 24))     ;; penetrations STILL unresolved after the last iteration
(define *phys-slot-maxresid* (new 'static 'array float 24))  ;; deepest residual penetration (window)
(define *phys-slot-rootdev* (new 'static 'array float 24))   ;; max drift of a LOCKED link, read back from the bone (must be 0)
(define *phys-slot-freeroot* (new 'static 'array float 24))  ;; max drift of an UNLOCKED link-0 (contrast: proves the sim is live)
(define *phys-slot-reglue* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; chains whose authored channel was replaced this frame
(define *phys-slot-desc* (new 'static 'array int32 24))      ;; non-simulated descendants re-glued onto moved parents (anti-tear)
(define *phys-slot-nopose* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; chain-frames with a ZERO-LENGTH pose (parked spawn / teleport frame) — not simulatable, not audited
;; ---- cycle-3 counters -------------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-slot-authhold* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; (A) chain-frames the AUTHORED animation owned (blend > 0.5)
(define *phys-slot-autheng* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; (A) suspension ENGAGE events
(define *phys-slot-authrel* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; (A) suspension RELEASE events (physics resumed) — engage without release = stuck
(define *phys-slot-authmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))   ;; (A) max blend weight reached
(define *phys-slot-reseed* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; (B) spawn + teleport chain resets
(define *phys-slot-burst* (new 'static 'array int32 24))     ;; (B) settle frames whose VISIBLE deviation still blew past the bound — owner bar: 0
(define *phys-slot-frozen* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; (D) ACTIVE chains that never moved in a window where the actor did

;; ---- cycle-3 constants ------------------------------------------------------------------------
(defconstant PHYS-SETTLE 20)          ;; frames of physics ramp-in after a spawn / teleport (~1/3 s)
(defconstant PHYS-JUMP-ABS 4096.0)    ;; 1 m of anchor travel in ONE frame is a cut/teleport, never running
(defconstant PHYS-JUMP-REL 1.5)       ;; ...or 1.5x the chain's own length, whichever is larger
(defconstant PHYS-BURST-REL 0.35)     ;; a settling chain deviating past 35% of its length = "it went wild"
(defconstant PHYS-FROZEN-DEV 6.0)     ;; window deviation under this (1.5 mm) = the chain never moved
(defconstant PHYS-FROZEN-ANCH 60.0)   ;; ...and only counts in a window where the anchor really did move

;; WAVE 2: the sim no longer reads a companion's khd-par — every slot carries its OWN parent table,
;; filled either from the companion's k->e table or, for a stock rider, from the live jgeo
;; (joint.parent). 255 = root / out of range.
(define *phys-par* (new 'static 'array uint8 3072))     ;; PHYS-SLOTS * PHYS-MAXJ
(define *phys-slot-rider* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; 1 = stock-model rider slot
(define *phys-slot-stamp* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; frame this slot last stepped (rider GC +
                                                         ;; once-per-frame guard)
(define *phys-slot-gen* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; params generation the slot was bound with

;; per sim joint (idx = slot*PHYS-JPS + j)
(define *phys-jk* (new 'static 'array int32 1152))          ;; rig joint index k
(define *phys-pos* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
(define *phys-prev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
(define *phys-targ* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152)) ;; per-frame target cache
(define *phys-anim* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152)) ;; per-frame AUTHORED position (pre re-glue), for anim=excite and (A) authored priority
(define *phys-jdev* (new 'static 'array float 1152))         ;; (D) per-LINK window max deviation: "only the tip moves" is a number, not an impression

;; per chain (idx = slot*PHYS-CPS + c); cstart is the joint index base WITHIN the slot.
(define *phys-cstart* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-clen* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-cflags* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-canchor* (new 'static 'array int32 576))      ;; anchor rig joint index (link0's parent)
(define *phys-comega* (new 'static 'array float 576))       ;; 2*pi*hz
(define *phys-cdamp* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cgrav* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; gravity scale
(define *phys-cmaxrad* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; swing cone half-angle, RADIANS (per-link scaled by the gradient)
(define *phys-cinertia* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cstretch* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cradius* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; per-joint collision radius
(define *phys-crootlock* (new 'static 'array int32 576))    ;; leading links pinned rigidly to the animated bone
(define *phys-cgrad* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; 0 = uniform, 1 = full root->tip freedom ramp
(define *phys-canim* (new 'static 'array int32 576))        ;; 0 keep / 1 replace / 2 excite
(define *phys-cexcite* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; anim=excite: authored-delta force scale
(define *phys-cfric* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; contact friction 0..1
(define *phys-cdev* (new 'static 'array float 576))         ;; window max deviation OF THIS CHAIN (per-chain proof)
;; ---- cycle-3 per-chain state ------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-cauth* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; (A) authored-priority blend weight, 0 = pure physics, 1 = the animator owns the chain
(define *phys-cauththr* (new 'static 'array float 576))     ;; (A) engage threshold (authored offset / chain length); 0 = feature off for this chain
(define *phys-cauthrise* (new 'static 'array float 576))    ;; (A) blend-in rate per second
(define *phys-cauthfall* (new 'static 'array float 576))    ;; (A) blend-out rate per second — this is the "physics resumes progressively" ramp
(define *phys-cauthstiff* (new 'static 'array float 576))   ;; (A) stiffness multiplier at w=1 (how hard the chain tracks the authored pose)
(define *phys-cauthmax* (new 'static 'array float 576))     ;; (A) window max authored ratio seen — proves the DETECTOR is live even when it never engages
(define *phys-crootfree* (new 'static 'array float 576))    ;; (D) floor of the root->tip freedom ramp
(define *phys-cnodesc* (new 'static 'array int32 576))      ;; descendants of this chain carry their OWN animation — do not rigid-re-glue them
(define *phys-csettle* (new 'static 'array int32 576))      ;; (B) frames of physics ramp-in left after a spawn / teleport
(define *phys-canchprev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 576)) ;; (B) this chain's anchor last frame — a one-frame jump IS the teleport signal
(define *phys-cpush* (new 'static 'array int32 576))        ;; per-chain collision push-outs (window): names the chain a collider is WELDING

;; body collision volumes (idx = slot*PHYS-COLS + i). joint2 < 0 = sphere on joint1, else CAPSULE
;; swept between the two animated bones.
(define *phys-colk* (new 'static 'array int32 384))         ;; jgeo joint index carrying the volume
(define *phys-colk2* (new 'static 'array int32 384))        ;; capsule far end, -1 = sphere
(define *phys-colr* (new 'static 'array float 384))
(define *phys-colr2* (new 'static 'array float 384))        ;; (C) far-end radius: radius != radius2 = a TAPERED (conical) volume
(define *phys-colmask* (new 'static 'array int64 384))      ;; chain-applicability bits (bit c)
(define *phys-coltier* (new 'static 'array int32 384))      ;; 1 = core (every level), 2 = extended

;; gravity: 9.8 m/s^2 * 4096 units/m
(defconstant PHYS-GRAV-ACCEL 40140.8)

(defun phys-closest-on-seg! ((out vector) (a vector) (b vector) (p vector))
  "closest point of a collider's SPINE to p. A sphere passes b = a (the degenerate segment falls
  through to `a`), a capsule passes its two animated bone positions — one code path, so the
  constraint pass and the residual audit can never drift apart.
  RETURNS the segment parameter t in [0,1] of that closest point (0 for the degenerate/sphere case)
  so a TAPERED capsule (cycle 3, owner C) can interpolate its radius AT THE CONTACT — a cone. Both
  callers must use the same t or the audit would grade the push-out against a different volume."
  (let ((tt 0.0))
    (let ((ab (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
          (ap (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
      (vector-! ab b a)
      (let ((d2 (vector-dot ab ab)))
        (cond
          ((< d2 0.0001)
           (vector-copy! out a))
          (else
           (vector-! ap p a)
           (set! tt (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (/ (vector-dot ap ab) d2))))
           (vector-float*! ab ab tt)
           (vector+! out a ab)))))
    tt))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; WAVE 2 slot pool. A "slot" is one simulated ACTOR: its parent table, its chains, its verlet
;; state. Nothing in here knows what kind of process owns it — that is the whole point of wave 2.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defun phys-slot-find ((pid int))
  "the sim slot bound to this process, or -1."
  (let ((r -1))
    (dotimes (s PHYS-SLOTS)
      (when (and (< r 0) (= (-> *phys-slot-pid* s) pid))
        (set! r s)))
    r))

(defun phys-slot-free! ((slot int))
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-pid* slot) 0)
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot) 0)
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot) 0)
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot) 0)
  (none))

(defun phys-slot-claim ((pid int) (rider? int))
  "claim a free slot. Companions take the bottom of the pool ascending, riders the top descending,
  so a crowded village can never starve an HD companion. Rider slots are reclaimed by AGE: a stock
  actor is a plain process-drawable with no deactivate hook of ours, so a slot whose owner stopped
  stepping for a few frames is dead by definition."
  (let ((r -1))
    (cond
      ((zero? rider?)
       (dotimes (s PHYS-COMP-SLOTS)
         (when (and (< r 0) (zero? (-> *phys-slot-pid* s)))
           (set! r s))))
      (else
       (let ((now (the int (current-time))))
         ;; reap stale riders first
         (dotimes (i (- PHYS-SLOTS PHYS-COMP-SLOTS))
           (let ((s (- (- PHYS-SLOTS 1) i)))
             (when (and (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-pid* s))
                        (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-rider* s))
                        (> (- now (-> *phys-slot-stamp* s)) 8))
               (phys-slot-free! s)))))
       (dotimes (i (- PHYS-SLOTS PHYS-COMP-SLOTS))
         (let ((s (- (- PHYS-SLOTS 1) i)))
           (when (and (< r 0) (zero? (-> *phys-slot-pid* s)))
             (set! r s))))))
    (when (>= r 0)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-pid* r) pid)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-rider* r) rider?)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* r) (the int (current-time))))
    r))

(defun phys-fill-par-from-table! ((slot int) (par (pointer uint8)) (n int))
  "companion path: copy the k->e prep table's HD parent column into the slot."
  (let ((pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ)))
    (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ n))
      (set! (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)) (-> par k))))
  (none))

(defun phys-fill-par-from-jgeo! ((slot int) (jgeo art-joint-geo) (n int))
  "rider path: the STOCK rig carries its own hierarchy — `joint.parent` is a pointer to the parent
  joint and `joint.number` is that joint's index into jgeo data (this is exactly what
  make-nodes-from-jg uses to wire the cspaces). No offline table, no prep step: any actor in the
  game can be simulated the frame it spawns."
  (let ((pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ)))
    (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ n))
      (let ((j (-> jgeo data k))
            (p 255))
        (when (-> j parent)
          (let ((pn (-> j parent number)))
            (when (and (>= pn 0) (< pn PHYS-MAXJ))
              (set! p pn))))
        (set! (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)) (the uint8 p)))))
  (none))

(defun phys-slot-bind! ((slot int) (draw draw-control) (ag string) (rig int))
  "resolve ONE actor's chains from the data file against its live jgeo, into an already-claimed
  slot. Joint names -> (chain,link) via pc-physics-joint-role; the chain ORDER is then derived from
  the rig's own parent table (*phys-par*, filled by the caller from the companion prep table or
  straight from the jgeo), and link0's parent becomes the animated anchor.
  RIG-AGNOSTIC BY CONSTRUCTION: `ag` is just the params key (a companion art-group name for an HD
  companion, the JOINT-GEO name for a stock rider) and `rig` is just the joint count — nothing here
  touches jak-hd. That is what lets the same solver run on every actor in the game."
  (let* ((jgeo (-> draw jgeo))
         (nch (min PHYS-CPS (pc-physics-num-chains ag)))
         (jbase (* slot PHYS-JPS))
         (cbase (* slot PHYS-CPS))
         (pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ))
         (nj (min PHYS-MAXJ rig))
         (njoints 0)
         (ncols 0)
         (ndropped 0)
         (nreorder 0)
         ;; temp role tables indexed by rig joint k (k < PHYS-MAXJ by construction)
         (tchain (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 128))
         (tlink (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 128))
         ;; per-chain member SET and the order derived from the rig (both <= PHYS-JPS)
         (mem (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 48))
         (ord (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 48)))
    ;; a rig deeper than the parent-table ceiling is not a crash, but the chains cannot reference
    ;; anything past it — say so once, at bind time, instead of dropping those joints in silence.
    (when (> rig PHYS-MAXJ)
      (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S rig has ~D joints > ~D — joints past the ceiling cannot be chained~%"
              ag rig PHYS-MAXJ))
    ;; resolve every rig joint's role once
    (dotimes (k nj)
      (set! (-> tchain k) -1)
      (set! (-> tlink k) -1)
      (when (< k (-> jgeo length))
        (let ((role (pc-physics-joint-role ag (-> jgeo data k name))))
          (when (>= role 0)
            (set! (-> tchain k) (shr role 8))
            (set! (-> tlink k) (logand role #xff))))))
    ;; ---- chain build: the joint list is a SET, the ORDER comes from the RIG --------------------
    ;; The declared `j` order in physics_chains.txt is the AUTHOR's intent, but for stock NPC rigs
    ;; nobody can verify root->tip order offline: the shipped art files carry the hierarchy, not our
    ;; config. Requiring the declared order to match exactly meant one wrong line silently disabled a
    ;; whole character. So the chain's joint list is treated as a SET and the order is derived from the
    ;; rig itself: the member whose parent is not a member is the root, then each next link is the
    ;; unique member parented to the previous one. A set that is not a single parent-child path is a
    ;; data bug and is dropped LOUDLY. For every chain that already validated (all HD companions) the
    ;; derived order is identical to the declared one, so this is strictly a superset.
    (dotimes (c nch)
      (let ((ci (+ cbase c))
            (start njoints)
            (len 0)
            (bad 0)
            (nmem 0))
        ;; (1) members: every joint of THIS rig the data file assigns to chain c.
        (dotimes (k nj)
          (when (= (-> tchain k) c)
            (cond
              ((>= nmem PHYS-JPS)
               (set! bad 1))
              (else
               (set! (-> mem nmem) k)
               (+! nmem 1)))))
        (when (and (> nmem 0) (zero? bad))
          ;; (2) the root is the single member whose parent lies OUTSIDE the set (255, out of range,
          ;; or simply not a member). Two roots means the config lumped two chains into one entry.
          (let ((root -1)
                (nroots 0))
            (dotimes (i nmem)
              (let ((p (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase (-> mem i)))))
                    (inset 0))
                (when (and (!= p #xff) (< p nj))
                  (dotimes (j nmem)
                    (when (= (-> mem j) p)
                      (set! inset 1))))
                (when (zero? inset)
                  (+! nroots 1)
                  (when (< root 0)
                    (set! root (-> mem i))))))
            (cond
              ((!= nroots 1)
               (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid: ~D roots in the rig — not a single chain~%"
                       ag c nroots)
               (set! bad 1))
              (else
               ;; (3) walk root->tip: at every step EXACTLY one member must hang off the current one.
               (set! (-> ord 0) root)
               (let ((n 1))
                 (while (and (< n nmem) (zero? bad))
                   (let ((cur (-> ord (+ n -1)))
                         (nxt -1)
                         (nkids 0))
                     (dotimes (i nmem)
                       (when (= (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase (-> mem i)))) cur)
                         (+! nkids 1)
                         (when (< nxt 0)
                           (set! nxt (-> mem i)))))
                     (cond
                       ((> nkids 1)
                        (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid: branches at link ~D (declare one chain per branch)~%"
                                ag c (+ n -1))
                        (set! bad 1))
                       ((< nxt 0)
                        (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid: only ~D of ~D joints connect — not a single chain~%"
                                ag c n nmem)
                        (set! bad 1))
                       (else
                        (set! (-> ord n) nxt)
                        (+! n 1))))))
               ;; (4) anchor = the root's parent: an ANIMATED bone the sim reads and never writes.
               (when (zero? bad)
                 (let ((anc (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase root)))))
                   (cond
                     ((or (= anc #xff) (>= anc rig))
                      (set! bad 1))
                     (else
                      (set! (-> *phys-canchor* ci) anc)))))
               ;; (5) slot capacity
               (when (and (zero? bad) (> (+ njoints nmem) PHYS-JPS))
                 (set! bad 1))
               (when (zero? bad)
                 ;; (6) declared-vs-derived: link i of the file must BE the i-th joint of the walk.
                 ;; When it is not, the rig wins and the mismatch is named — a re-order is a config
                 ;; bug the author still wants to hear about, not a silent correction.
                 (let ((diff 0))
                   (dotimes (i nmem)
                     (when (!= (-> tlink (-> ord i)) i)
                       (set! diff 1)))
                   (when (nonzero? diff)
                     (+! nreorder 1)
                     (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D re-ordered from the rig hierarchy (declared order did not match)~%"
                             ag c)))
                 ;; (7) commit, root->tip
                 (dotimes (i nmem)
                   (set! (-> *phys-jk* (+ jbase njoints)) (-> ord i))
                   (+! njoints 1)
                   (+! len 1)))))))
        (when (nonzero? bad)
          (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid (order/anchor/capacity) — disabled~%" ag c)
          (set! njoints start)
          (set! len 0))
        ;; CYCLE 2 (defects C/D): a chain whose joint NAMES resolve to nothing in the live rig
        ;; used to vanish in silence — indistinguishable from "simulated but too subtle". Name
        ;; it, loudly, and count it: a dropped chain is a data bug, never a tuning problem.
        ;; WAVE 2: only the NAMES-not-in-this-rig case prints this line. A chain killed by the
        ;; hierarchy checks above already printed its own specific reason, and stacking a
        ;; "0 of its joints exist" on top of it would send the reader hunting a typo that is not
        ;; there. Both still count as dropped.
        (when (zero? len)
          (+! ndropped 1)
          (when (zero? nmem)
            (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D DROPPED: 0 of its joints exist in this rig~%" ag c)))
        (set! (-> *phys-cstart* ci) start)
        (set! (-> *phys-clen* ci) len)
        (set! (-> *phys-cflags* ci) (pc-physics-chain-flags ag c))
        (set! (-> *phys-cdev* ci) 0.0)
        ;; params (milli -> float) + derived
        (let ((hz (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 0))))
              (maxang (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 3)))))
          (set! (-> *phys-comega* ci) (* 6.2831855 hz))
          (set! (-> *phys-cdamp* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 1))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cgrav* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 2))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cmaxrad* ci) (* 0.017453292 maxang))
          (set! (-> *phys-cinertia* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 4))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cstretch* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 5))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cradius* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 6))))
          ;; cycle 2: root lock / freedom gradient / authored-channel mode / contact friction
          (set! (-> *phys-crootlock* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 7) 1000))
          (set! (-> *phys-cgrad* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 8))))
          (set! (-> *phys-canim* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 9) 1000))
          (set! (-> *phys-cexcite* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 10))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cfric* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 11))))
          ;; cycle 3: authored-animation priority / freedom floor / descendant policy
          (set! (-> *phys-cauththr* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 12))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthrise* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 13))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthfall* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 14))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthstiff* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 15))))
          (set! (-> *phys-crootfree* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 16))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cnodesc* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 17) 1000))
          ;; a re-bind (hot params push, look switch) must not inherit a half-engaged suspension or a
          ;; stale anchor: every chain starts calm, at rest, and SETTLES in (owner B).
          (set! (-> *phys-cauth* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthmax* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cpush* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-csettle* ci) PHYS-SETTLE)
          (vector-reset! (-> *phys-canchprev* ci)))))
    ;; body collision volumes: file order, joints resolved by name, per-chain applicability
    ;; mask + tier. A capsule needs BOTH ends present in the rig or it degrades to a sphere on
    ;; its first joint (never silently: the drop is logged).
    (let ((ncf (min PHYS-COLS (pc-physics-num-colliders ag))))
      (dotimes (i ncf)
        (let ((found -1)
              (found2 -1)
              (cap? (= 1 (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 3))))
          (dotimes (k (-> jgeo length))
            (when (and (< found 0) (> (pc-physics-collider-is-joint ag i (-> jgeo data k name)) 0))
              (set! found k))
            (when (and cap? (< found2 0)
                       (> (pc-physics-collider-is-joint2 ag i (-> jgeo data k name)) 0))
              (set! found2 k)))
          (cond
            ((< found 0)
             (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S collider ~D DROPPED: its joint is not in this rig~%" ag i))
            (else
             (when (and cap? (< found2 0))
               (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S capsule ~D far end missing — degraded to a sphere~%" ag i))
             (let ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS) ncols)))
               (set! (-> *phys-colk* cb) found)
               (set! (-> *phys-colk2* cb) (if cap? found2 -1))
               (set! (-> *phys-colr* cb) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 0))))
               (set! (-> *phys-colmask* cb) (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 1))
               (set! (-> *phys-coltier* cb) (max 1 (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 2))))
             (+! ncols 1))))))
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot) njoints)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot) nch)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot) ncols)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot) 0)
    ;; HOT-RELOAD BOOKKEEPING: the generation this binding was produced from. phys-slot-step!
    ;; compares it every frame and re-binds when the owner pushes a new physics_chains.txt or
    ;; flips the precision level — companions AND riders, without respawning anything.
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-gen* slot) (pc-physics-generation))
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot) (the int (current-time)))
    ;; ONE LINE, always: GOAL caps a call at 8 parameters (format + dest + fmt + 6 args is already
    ;; the ceiling), and every `format 0` is its own logcat line on Android — so the two wave-2
    ;; fields are APPENDED through the shared string buffer instead of splitting the init line and
    ;; disarming every line-based device gate that greps it.
    (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
            "[HD-PHYS] init ag=~S slot=~D chains=~D dropped=~D sim-joints=~D colliders=~D"
            ag slot nch ndropped njoints ncols)
    (format *phys-line-buf* " reorder=~D rider=~D" nreorder (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot))
    (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*))
  (none))

(defun phys-slot-step! ((slot int) (draw draw-control) (ag string) (rig int))
  "the per-frame verlet/spring chain sim for ONE bound slot. For an HD companion it runs after
  fill-jak-hd-bones! — the freshly retargeted world matrices are the spring targets (or, under
  anim=replace/excite, the re-glued BIND-POSE matrices carried by the animated anchor). For a stock
  actor the same matrices come straight out of do-joint-math!. Either way the bones are FINAL and
  world-space when we get here, and the slot's own parent table (*phys-par*) says who hangs off
  whom — so this body never needs to know which kind of process owns the rig. See the file header
  for the algorithm."
  ;; hot-reload: pc-set-physics! re-parses physics_chains.txt whenever the owner flips the menu
  ;; toggle or the precision level, which bumps the generation. Re-binding here means a pushed
  ;; params file takes effect on companions AND riders without respawning anything.
  (let ((g (pc-physics-generation)))
    (when (!= g (-> *phys-slot-gen* slot))
      (phys-slot-bind! slot draw ag rig)))
  (let ((en (pc-physics-enabled)))
    (when (and (> en 0) (> (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot) 0)
               (nonzero? draw) (nonzero? (-> draw skeleton))
               (nonzero? (-> draw jgeo)))
      (let* ((level (+ en -1))
             (skel (-> draw skeleton))
             (hd-jgeo (-> draw jgeo))
             (nbones (-> skel length))
             (jbase (* slot PHYS-JPS))
             (cbase (* slot PHYS-CPS))
             (pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ))
             (substeps (max 1 (min 8 (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 0) 1000))))
             (iters (max 1 (min 16 (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 1) 1000))))
             ;; cycle 2: `collide` is a TIER now, not a bool — 0 = no collisions, 1 = core volumes
             ;; only, 2 = the full body set. The lowest level still collides (owner 17:35: a level
             ;; may thin the collider set, never let a chain visibly pass through the body).
             (tier (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 2) 1000))
             (classmask (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 3) 1000))
             (fixedhz (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 4))))
             (dt (seconds-per-frame))
             ;; temps hoisted out of all loops (GOAL stack allocs accumulate per call frame)
             (vtmp (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (vtmp2 (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (vtmp3 (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (cpt (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (axis (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (dirv (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (dirt (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (dirs (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (q (new 'stack-no-clear 'quaternion))
             (rotm (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             (tmpm (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             (hbind (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             (lkm (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             ;; per-link freedom ladder, recomputed per chain per frame (<= PHYS-JPS entries)
             (lo2 (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'float 48))
             (lcos (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'float 48))
             (lsin (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'float 48))
             ;; per-rig-joint "this bone moved this frame" flag, for the descendant pass (k < PHYS-MAXJ)
             (moved (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 128))
             (frame-maxvel 0.0)
             (frame-maxdev 0.0)
             (frame-nact 0)
             (frame-nreglue 0)
             (frame-ndesc 0)
             (frame-nopose 0))
        (when (and (> dt 0.0001) (< dt 0.1))
          ;; fixed-timestep ladder top: substep count from the accumulator target rate
          (when (> fixedhz 1.0)
            (set! substeps (max 1 (min 8 (the int (+ 0.5 (* dt fixedhz)))))))
          (let ((sdt (/ dt (the float substeps))))
            ;; ---------------- (A) authored-channel neutralization, BEFORE the targets are cached --
            ;; For every ACTIVE chain in anim=replace/excite: stash the authored world position, then
            ;; re-glue the joint to its BIND-POSE local carried by its parent. From here on the
            ;; target IS the calm rest pose rigidly attached to the animated anchor, so the fake wind
            ;; and the sim can never both write the bone — the sim is the only secondary motion.
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                     (len (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                     (start (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci))))
                (when (and (> len 0) (> (-> *phys-canim* ci) 0)
                           (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask)))
                  (+! frame-nreglue 1)
                  (dotimes (i len)
                    (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i))))
                      (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                        (vector-copy! (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i))
                                      (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3))
                        (let ((p (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)))))
                          (when (and (!= p #xff) (< (+ p 1) nbones))
                            ;; W'_k = L'_k . W'_par, L'_k = inv(bind-pose[k]) . bind-pose[par]
                            (matrix-4x4-inverse! hbind (-> hd-jgeo data k bind-pose))
                            (matrix*! lkm hbind (-> hd-jgeo data p bind-pose))
                            (matrix*! (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform) lkm
                                      (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ p 1) transform)))))))))))
            ;; cache this frame's targets (write-back overwrites bones; tips need pristine parents)
            (dotimes (j (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot))
              (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ jbase j))))
                (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                  (vector-copy! (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase j))
                                (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3)))))
            ;; debug instrument: does the driver pose move at all? (chain0 anchor world delta)
            (when (> (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot) 0)
              (let* ((a0 (-> *phys-canchor* cbase))
                     (ap (-> skel bones (+ a0 1) transform vector 3)))
                (when (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot))
                  (vector-! vtmp ap (-> *phys-slot-anchprev* slot))
                  (let ((am (vector-length vtmp)))
                    (when (> am (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot))
                      (set! (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot) am))))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-slot-anchprev* slot) ap)))
            ;; first frame (or post-reset spawn): seed at targets = start at rest
            (when (zero? (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot) 1)
              (dotimes (j (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ jbase j)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase j)))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ jbase j)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase j)))))
            ;; ---------------- integrate + constrain, per chain ----------------
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                     (len (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                     (start (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci)))
                     (active (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask))))
                (when (> len 0)
                  (cond
                    ((not active)
                     ;; chain class disabled at this level: ride rigidly (state pinned to targets)
                     (dotimes (i len)
                       (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                       (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))))
                    (else
                     (+! frame-nact 1)
                     (let* ((anchor-k (-> *phys-canchor* ci))
                            (anchor (-> skel bones (+ anchor-k 1) transform vector 3))
                            (omega (-> *phys-comega* ci))
                            (odt (* omega sdt))
                            ;; (B) never lock the whole chain: at least the tip stays free.
                            (rl (max 0 (min (+ len -1) (-> *phys-crootlock* ci))))
                            (nfree (- len rl))
                            (grad (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (-> *phys-cgrad* ci))))
                            ;; excite only means anything in mode 2 — in any other mode *phys-anim*
                            ;; was never filled for this chain and would feed stale positions in.
                            (exc (if (= 2 (-> *phys-canim* ci)) (-> *phys-cexcite* ci) 0.0))
                            (fric (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (-> *phys-cfric* ci))))
                            (rad0 (-> *phys-cradius* ci))
                            ;; POSE GUARD (cycle-2 measurement bug). A companion can be handed a
                            ;; frame with EVERY bone at the origin: the title-screen parked spawn,
                            ;; and the frame a warp/cutscene-cut teleports the driver (anchmove read
                            ;; ~998000 units = 243 m in one frame). Then every chain length is 0, the
                            ;; distance constraint takes its degenerate branch and never reaches the
                            ;; collision code, while the joint and the collider spine both sit at
                            ;; (0,0,0) — so the residual audit scored a "penetration" of exactly
                            ;; `rr` on every pair. That is an un-posed frame, not a body
                            ;; intersection: a chain with no length has no physics to audit.
                            (chainlen (let ((s 0.0))
                                        (dotimes (i len)
                                          (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))
                                                    (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1))))
                                          (set! s (+ s (vector-length vtmp))))
                                        s))
                            (collide? (and (> tier 0) (> rad0 0.0) (>= chainlen 1.0))))
                       (when (< chainlen 1.0)
                         (+! frame-nopose 1))
                       ;; stability clamp: omega*dt <= 1.0 per substep — the low ladder stays a
                       ;; light CLEAN approximation, never an unstable one.
                       (when (> odt 1.0)
                         (set! omega (/ 1.0 sdt)))
                       ;; (B) per-link freedom ramp root->tip. grad=0 -> uniform (pre-cycle-2
                       ;; behaviour). grad=1 -> the first free link keeps 1/nfree of the swing cone
                       ;; and is 1/f times stiffer, the tip keeps the full authored amplitude.
                       (dotimes (i len)
                         (let ((f 1.0))
                           (when (and (> nfree 1) (> grad 0.0) (>= i rl))
                             (set! f (- 1.0 (* grad (- 1.0 (/ (the float (+ (- i rl) 1))
                                                              (the float nfree)))))))
                           (let ((wi (/ omega (fmax f 0.2))))
                             (when (> (* wi sdt) 1.0)
                               (set! wi (/ 1.0 sdt)))
                             (set! (-> lo2 i) (* wi wi)))
                           (let ((ang (* (-> *phys-cmaxrad* ci) f)))
                             (set! (-> lcos i) (cos-rad ang))
                             (set! (-> lsin i) (sin-rad ang)))))
                       ;; (B) locked links ride the animated bone rigidly: pin the state so the free
                       ;; links hang off a solid parent, and skip them everywhere below.
                       (dotimes (i rl)
                         (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                         (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))))
                       (let ((kd (/ (-> *phys-cinertia* ci) (+ 1.0 (* (-> *phys-cdamp* ci) sdt 60.0))))
                             (gacc (* (-> *phys-cgrav* ci) PHYS-GRAV-ACCEL)))
                         (dotimes (st substeps)
                           ;; verlet integrate every FREE link
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (let ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))
                                     (pv (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)))
                                     (tg (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))))
                                 ;; acc = o2*(t-p) + g  [+ excite*o2*(authored - t)]
                                 (vector-! vtmp tg p)
                                 (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (-> lo2 i))
                                 (set! (-> vtmp y) (- (-> vtmp y) gacc))
                                 (when (> exc 0.0)
                                   ;; (A) anim=excite: the authored channel we removed comes back as
                                   ;; an input FORCE only. exc=1 reproduces springing at the authored
                                   ;; pose exactly, so the mode is monotone and never a second writer.
                                   (vector-! vtmp3 (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i)) tg)
                                   (vector-float*! vtmp3 vtmp3 (* exc (-> lo2 i)))
                                   (vector+! vtmp vtmp vtmp3))
                                 ;; vel = (p - prev)*kd
                                 (vector-! vtmp2 p pv)
                                 (vector-float*! vtmp2 vtmp2 kd)
                                 (vector-copy! pv p)
                                 ;; p += vel + acc*sdt^2
                                 (vector+! p p vtmp2)
                                 (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (* sdt sdt))
                                 (vector+! p p vtmp))))
                           ;; constraint iterations
                           (dotimes (it iters)
                             (dotimes (i len)
                               (when (>= i rl)
                                 (let* ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))
                                        (tg (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                        (pp (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i -1))))
                                        (tp (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1)))))
                                   ;; rest length from LIVE targets (rig-scale robust)
                                   (vector-! axis tg tp)
                                   (let ((rest (vector-length axis)))
                                     (vector-! dirv p pp)
                                     (let ((dl (vector-length dirv)))
                                       (cond
                                         ((or (< dl 0.0001) (< rest 0.0001))
                                          ;; degenerate: pin to target
                                          (vector-copy! p tg))
                                         (else
                                          ;; distance constraint with allowed stretch
                                          (let* ((str (-> *phys-cstretch* ci))
                                                 (lmin (* rest (- 1.0 str)))
                                                 (lmax (* rest (+ 1.0 str)))
                                                 (dl2 (fmax lmin (fmin lmax dl))))
                                            (vector-float*! dirv dirv (/ dl2 dl))
                                            ;; cone limit around the target direction (per-link)
                                            (vector-float*! axis axis (/ 1.0 rest))
                                            (vector-float*! vtmp dirv (/ 1.0 dl2))
                                            (let ((dot (vector-dot vtmp axis))
                                                  (cmax (-> lcos i)))
                                              (when (< dot cmax)
                                                ;; decompose and re-aim at the cone boundary
                                                (vector-float*! vtmp2 axis dot)
                                                (vector-! vtmp2 vtmp vtmp2)
                                                (let ((pl (vector-length vtmp2)))
                                                  (cond
                                                    ((< pl 0.000001)
                                                     (vector-copy! vtmp axis))
                                                    (else
                                                     (vector-float*! vtmp2 vtmp2 (/ (-> lsin i) pl))
                                                     (vector-float*! vtmp axis cmax)
                                                     (vector+! vtmp vtmp vtmp2))))
                                                (vector-float*! dirv vtmp dl2)))
                                            (vector+! p pp dirv)
                                            ;; ---- body volumes (spheres + capsules, tier-gated) ----
                                            (when collide?
                                              (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot))
                                                (let ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS) s2)))
                                                  (when (and (<= (-> *phys-coltier* cb) tier)
                                                             (logtest? (-> *phys-colmask* cb) (ash 1 c)))
                                                    (let* ((k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb))
                                                           (ca (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3))
                                                           (cbv (if (>= k2 0)
                                                                    (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                                                                    ca))
                                                           (rr (+ (-> *phys-colr* cb) rad0)))
                                                      (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv p)
                                                      (vector-! vtmp p cpt)
                                                      (let ((dd (vector-length vtmp)))
                                                        (when (< dd rr)
                                                          (+! (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot) 1)
                                                          (let ((pen (- rr dd)))
                                                            (when (> pen (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot))
                                                              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot) pen)))
                                                          ;; push out to the surface...
                                                          (vector-copy! vtmp2 p)
                                                          ;; DEGENERATE (joint sitting exactly on the
                                                          ;; volume's spine): there is no push-out
                                                          ;; direction to normalize. Skipping it here
                                                          ;; would leave the joint inside the body
                                                          ;; forever AND make the residual audit below
                                                          ;; report a penetration no tuning could ever
                                                          ;; clear. Aim at the joint's own target
                                                          ;; instead, and straight up as a last resort.
                                                          (when (< dd 0.0001)
                                                            (vector-! vtmp tg cpt)
                                                            (set! dd (vector-length vtmp))
                                                            (when (< dd 0.0001)
                                                              (set! (-> vtmp x) 0.0)
                                                              (set! (-> vtmp y) 1.0)
                                                              (set! (-> vtmp z) 0.0)
                                                              (set! (-> vtmp w) 0.0)
                                                              (set! dd 1.0)))
                                                          (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (/ rr dd))
                                                          (vector+! p cpt vtmp)
                                                          ;; ...and absorb the push-out into `prev`
                                                          ;; (contact friction): without this the
                                                          ;; projection reads as free velocity next
                                                          ;; substep and the chain buzzes on contact.
                                                          (when (> fric 0.0)
                                                            (vector-! vtmp2 p vtmp2)
                                                            (vector-float*! vtmp2 vtmp2 fric)
                                                            (vector+! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i))
                                                                      (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) vtmp2)))))))))))))))))))
                         ;; ---- residual penetration audit (owner 17:35 bar: this must read 0) ----
                         ;; Measured AFTER the last iteration, on the state that is about to be
                         ;; written to the bones — a push-out counter alone would happily report
                         ;; thousands of resolutions while the chain still ends the frame inside the
                         ;; body. Locked links are excluded: they ARE the body, by construction.
                         (when collide?
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (let ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i))))
                                 (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot))
                                   (let ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS) s2)))
                                     (when (and (<= (-> *phys-coltier* cb) tier)
                                                (logtest? (-> *phys-colmask* cb) (ash 1 c)))
                                       (let* ((k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb))
                                              (ca (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3))
                                              (cbv (if (>= k2 0)
                                                       (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                                                       ca))
                                              (rr (+ (-> *phys-colr* cb) rad0)))
                                         (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv p)
                                         (vector-! vtmp p cpt)
                                         (let ((dd (vector-length vtmp)))
                                           ;; TOLERANCE: the push-out sets |p - cpt| = rr in float32,
                                           ;; and re-measuring it lands ~1e-4 relative below that
                                           ;; (measured: 0.03-0.08 units on radii of 400-800). A
                                           ;; residual only means something if it is deeper than that
                                           ;; noise floor. 1 unit = 0.24 mm on a 2.3 m character, so
                                           ;; nothing visible can hide under it.
                                           (when (< dd (- rr 1.0))
                                             (+! (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot) 1)
                                             (let ((pen (- rr dd)))
                                               (when (> pen (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot))
                                                 (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot) pen)))))))))))))
                         ;; ---------------- sanity + write-back ----------------
                         (let ((broken 0))
                           ;; chainlen is already computed above (the pose guard needs it first)
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (let ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i))))
                               (vector-! vtmp p (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                               (let ((dev (vector-length vtmp)))
                                 ;; NaN compares false on every test -> lands in the reset branch
                                 (when (not (and (< dev (+ 100.0 (* 2.0 chainlen)))
                                                 (< (fabs (-> p x)) 100000000.0)
                                                 (< (fabs (-> p y)) 100000000.0)
                                                 (< (fabs (-> p z)) 100000000.0)))
                                   (set! broken 1)))))
                           (cond
                             ((nonzero? broken)
                              ;; hard reset: pin the whole chain back to the targets this frame.
                              (+! (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot) 1)
                              (dotimes (i len)
                                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))))
                             (else
                              ;; write back root->tip: swing the 3x3 rows by (target-dir -> sim-dir),
                              ;; translation row = simulated position. Child targets read from the
                              ;; pristine *phys-targ* cache.
                              (dotimes (i len)
                                (cond
                                  ((< i rl)
                                   ;; (B) LOCKED link: no write-back at all — the bone keeps the
                                   ;; rigid re-glued rest transform, so the root of a hair chain
                                   ;; follows the skull exactly. Read the drift back FROM THE BONE
                                   ;; (not from the sim state) so the number would catch any other
                                   ;; writer touching it this frame. Owner bar: rootdev = 0.
                                   (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i))))
                                     (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                                       (vector-! vtmp (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3)
                                                 (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                       (let ((d (vector-length vtmp)))
                                         (when (> d (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot))
                                           (set! (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot) d))))))
                                  (else
                                   (let* ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))
                                          (tg (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                          (k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i)))
                                          (dst (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform))))
                                     ;; stats
                                     (vector-! vtmp p tg)
                                     (let ((dev (vector-length vtmp)))
                                       (when (> dev frame-maxdev) (set! frame-maxdev dev))
                                       ;; per-chain deviation: an INERT chain now reads as its own
                                       ;; number instead of hiding under the slot-wide maximum
                                       ;; (defect C was invisible to the aggregate counters).
                                       (when (> dev (-> *phys-cdev* ci))
                                         (set! (-> *phys-cdev* ci) dev))
                                       ;; contrast metric for (B): how far an UNLOCKED root drifts.
                                       (when (and (zero? i) (> dev (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot)))
                                         (set! (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot) dev)))
                                     (vector-! vtmp p (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)))
                                     (let ((vel (vector-length vtmp)))
                                       (when (> vel frame-maxvel) (set! frame-maxvel vel)))
                                     ;; direction pair: to child if any, else from parent
                                     (cond
                                       ((< (+ i 1) len)
                                        (vector-! dirt (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i 1)) tg)
                                        (vector-! dirs (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i 1)) p))
                                       (else
                                        (vector-! dirt tg (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1))))
                                        (vector-! dirs p (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i -1))))))
                                     (let ((lt (vector-length dirt))
                                           (ls (vector-length dirs)))
                                       (cond
                                         ((and (> lt 0.0001) (> ls 0.0001))
                                          (vector-float*! dirt dirt (/ 1.0 lt))
                                          (vector-float*! dirs dirs (/ 1.0 ls))
                                          (let ((dot (vector-dot dirt dirs)))
                                            (cond
                                              ((> dot 0.99999)
                                               ;; no swing: just move the translation row
                                               (vector-copy! (-> dst vector 3) p)
                                               (set! (-> dst vector 3 w) 1.0))
                                              ((< dot -0.999)
                                               ;; degenerate 180deg (one-frame): skip rotation
                                               (vector-copy! (-> dst vector 3) p)
                                               (set! (-> dst vector 3 w) 1.0))
                                              (else
                                               (quaternion-from-two-vectors! q dirt dirs)
                                               (quaternion->matrix rotm q)
                                               (matrix*! tmpm dst rotm)
                                               (dotimes (r 3)
                                                 (vector-copy! (-> dst vector r) (-> tmpm vector r))
                                                 (set! (-> dst vector r w) 0.0))
                                               (vector-copy! (-> dst vector 3) p)
                                               (set! (-> dst vector 3 w) 1.0)))))
                                         (else
                                          (vector-copy! (-> dst vector 3) p)
                                          (set! (-> dst vector 3 w) 1.0))))))))))))))))))
            ;; ---------------- rigid descendants of the joints we moved ----------------
            ;; A simulated joint's NON-simulated children are filled by fill-jak-hd-bones! straight
            ;; from the DRIVER and never re-derived, so moving the parent TEARS them off. Keira's
            ;; goggles are the canonical case: the chain drives gogglesMid (2492 verts) while
            ;; gogglesLeft/gogglesRight — the lenses, ~87% of the goggle geometry — kept following
            ;; the driver's head. Simulating the bridge alone would have ripped the glasses apart,
            ;; which is why the accessory could never be switched on (owner defect D).
            ;; Fix: after the sim, re-glue every DESCENDANT of a moved joint onto its new parent
            ;; (W'_k = L'_k . W'_par, the mode-2 product). Joints of class-gated chains are NOT
            ;; marked moved (their bones were never touched), so a lower precision level cannot
            ;; silently drop a descendant's authored animation.
            (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ rig))
              (set! (-> moved k) 0))
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let ((ci (+ cbase c)))
                (when (and (> (-> *phys-clen* ci) 0)
                           (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask)))
                  (let ((rl (max 0 (min (+ (-> *phys-clen* ci) -1) (-> *phys-crootlock* ci)))))
                    (dotimes (i (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                      ;; a LOCKED link of a `keep` chain was never touched (no re-glue, no
                      ;; write-back), so it must NOT drag its children off their own animation.
                      (when (or (> (-> *phys-canim* ci) 0) (>= i rl))
                        (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci) i))))
                          (when (< k PHYS-MAXJ)
                            (set! (-> moved k) 1)))))))))
            ;; The HD k->e table guarantees parent index < child index, so ONE forward pass
            ;; propagated through whole sub-trees. Stock art files make no such promise (redsage
            ;; literally stores LarmFlapB before LarmFlapA), so a single pass would leave a
            ;; descendant torn off its moved parent. Three passes with an early exit costs nothing
            ;; and closes the hole for any rig.
            (let ((more 1))
              (dotimes (pass 3)
                (when (nonzero? more)
                  (set! more 0)
                  (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ rig))
                    (when (and (zero? (-> moved k)) (< (+ k 1) nbones))
                      (let ((p (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)))))
                        (when (and (!= p #xff) (< p PHYS-MAXJ) (< (+ p 1) nbones) (nonzero? (-> moved p)))
                          (matrix-4x4-inverse! hbind (-> hd-jgeo data k bind-pose))
                          (matrix*! lkm hbind (-> hd-jgeo data p bind-pose))
                          (matrix*! (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform) lkm
                                    (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ p 1) transform)))
                          ;; propagate: this bone moved too, so ITS children follow in the same pass
                          (set! (-> moved k) 1)
                          (set! more 1)
                          (+! frame-ndesc 1))))))))
            ;; ---------------- windowed proof counters ----------------
            (when (> frame-maxdev (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot) frame-maxdev))
            (when (> frame-maxvel (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot) frame-maxvel))
            (when (> frame-nreglue (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot) frame-nreglue))
            (when (> frame-ndesc (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot) frame-ndesc))
            (+! (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot) frame-nopose)
            ;; rest convergence: 30 consecutive calm frames -> the spring has settled back
            (cond
              ((< frame-maxvel 2.0)
               (+! (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 1)
               (when (= (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 30)
                 (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S rest-converged: restdev=~f (chain returned to rest)~%"
                         ag frame-maxdev)))
              (else
               (set! (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 0)))
            (+! (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 1)
            (when (>= (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 300)
              ;; A GOAL call carries at most 8 parameters, so the window needs several format calls —
              ;; but each `format 0` is routed to Android's log as its OWN logcat line, which split
              ;; the window across three lines on device and made every line-based device gate read
              ;; push=/maxpen= as ABSENT (cycle-5 measurement bug: the x86 stdout stream concatenated
              ;; them, the device stream did not). Build the whole window in a string buffer first
              ;; (format to a string APPENDS; clear starts it) and emit it with ONE call, so the
              ;; window is exactly ONE line on BOTH targets.
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S lvl=~D window: chains=~D joints=~D act=~D cm=~D"
                      ag
                      level
                      (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot)
                      frame-nact
                      classmask)
              (format *phys-line-buf*
                      " maxdev=~f maxvel=~f anchmove=~f nan-resets=~D (verlet state dump bounded)"
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot))
              ;; FIELD NAMING IS LOAD-BEARING: every device gate is a line-based grep, so no field
              ;; name may CONTAIN another's. `freeroot=` (not freerootdev=) and `residmax=` (not
              ;; maxresid=) exist precisely so `grep -v 'rootdev=0.0000 '` and `grep -v 'resid=0 '`
              ;; cannot match the wrong field and report a drifting root / residual penetration as
              ;; clean. Rename one of these and you silently disarm its gate.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " push=~D maxpen=~f resid=~D residmax=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot))
              ;; GOAL caps a call at 8 parameters (format + dest + fmt-string + 7 args = 9 = too
              ;; many), so this is two calls — which is FINE and is exactly why the whole window is
              ;; assembled in a string buffer: appending to a string does not split the line, only
              ;; `format 0` does.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " tier=~D cols=~D reglue=~D desc=~D nopose=~D"
                      tier
                      (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " rootdev=~f freeroot=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot))
              ;; per-chain window deviation — the whole list, never a top-N (a silent cap would read
              ;; as "every chain covered"). Same line, so line-based device gates still match.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cdev:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-cdev* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-cdev* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot) 0)))))))
  (none))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; HD COMPANION entry points. These three keep their exact names and signatures — jak-hd.gc calls
;; them from init-jak-hd / do-joint-math! / deactivate and knows nothing about the slot pool. All
;; the companion-specific knowledge (the k->e prep table, the *hd-ag-names* params key, hd-joints)
;; lives HERE and nowhere in the solver.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defun jak-hd-physics-init ((obj jak-hd))
  "claim a sim slot for this companion and resolve its chains from the data file against the live
  HD jgeo. The parent table comes from the generated k->e prep column (khd-par, 255 = root).
  Reload the params file on every init: pushing a new physics_chains.txt to the device then
  switching a LOOK (or toggling ENHANCED MODELS) re-reads everything — fast iteration."
  ;; cycle-2 defect E: prove the physics menu rows are still distinct from the mesh-browser
  ;; button. Done here because this runs on every companion spawn, physics toggle on OR off.
  (physics-menu-static-audit!)
  (when (and (nonzero? (-> obj draw)) (nonzero? (-> obj draw jgeo)))
    (let ((slot (phys-slot-claim (the int (-> obj pid)) 0)))
      (cond
        ((< slot 0)
         (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] no free sim slot — physics disabled for this companion~%"))
        (else
         (pc-physics-reload)
         (phys-fill-par-from-table! slot (-> obj khd-par) (-> obj hd-joints))
         (phys-slot-bind! slot (-> obj draw) (-> *hd-ag-names* (-> obj entry)) (-> obj hd-joints))))))
  (none))

(defun jak-hd-physics-step ((obj jak-hd))
  "the companion's per-frame step, called from its do-joint-math! override right after
  fill-jak-hd-bones!. Stamping the slot BEFORE the step is what makes the stock-actor rider's
  once-per-frame guard and its age-based slot reclamation work off a single counter."
  (let ((slot (phys-slot-find (the int (-> obj pid)))))
    (when (>= slot 0)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot) (the int (current-time)))
      (phys-slot-step! slot (-> obj draw) (-> *hd-ag-names* (-> obj entry)) (-> obj hd-joints))))
  (none))

(defun jak-hd-physics-release ((obj jak-hd))
  "free this companion's sim slot (called from deactivate)."
  (dotimes (s PHYS-SLOTS)
    (when (= (-> *phys-slot-pid* s) (the int (-> obj pid)))
      (phys-slot-free! s)))
  (none))

;; ================================================================================================
;; WAVE 2 (owner 2026-08-05 16:50 / 2026-08-06) — PHYSICS ON THE WHOLE CAST
;; ================================================================================================
;; The HD companions own a skeleton of their own; every OTHER character in jak1 is a stock
;; process-drawable with no companion and no prep step. The sim core above is rig-agnostic — it
;; resolves chains by joint NAME and walks a parent table — so a stock actor needs nothing but a
;; POST-ANIM HOOK: process-drawable::do-joint-math! calls phys-rider-post! once the bones are final,
;; and the same solver runs IN PLACE on the actor's own bones. This is the joint-mod-class hook the
;; phase spec asks for, at the one point in the frame where every rig is guaranteed posed.
;;
;; Chains are declared per RIG in physics_chains.txt keyed by the JOINT-GEO name ("sage-lod0-jg"):
;; jgeo is one object per art group and survives LOD switches, mgeo does not (lod-set! swaps it).
;;
;; NO bone injection is needed for the inherited sites — the shipped rigs already carry the chain
;; joints (Maia's 8-link ponytail, Gol's four capes, the geologist's braids, every sage's beard,
;; the fisherman's belly). Where a rig genuinely has no joint for an owner-listed site, that is
;; documented in the phase report with the evidence, never silently dropped.

(define *phys-cover-pid* (new 'static 'array int32 16))
(define *phys-cover-stamp* (new 'static 'array int32 16))
;; DISCOVERY LOG. The rider binds a stock actor by looking its RIG up in physics_chains.txt, and a
;; rig that is simply not in the file is indistinguishable, from the outside, from a rider that is
;; broken. So the first time each distinct rig is seen, name it and print the chain count the params
;; store answered with. `chains=0` = that character has no config yet (a data question);
;; nothing at all = the hook never ran (a code question). Keyed on the jgeo POINTER purely to avoid
;; repeating the line — a stale pointer after a level unload costs one extra log line, nothing else.
(defconstant PHYS-RIDER-SEEN 40)
(define *phys-seen-jgeo* (new 'static 'array int32 40))
(define *phys-seen-n* 0)
(define *phys-rider-bound* 0)     ;; rider slots bound this session
(define *phys-rider-full* 0)      ;; slot-starvation events
(define *phys-rider-active* 0)    ;; rider steps in the current window
(define *phys-rider-frames* 0)
(define *phys-rider-last* 0)

(defun phys-note-covered! ((pid int))
  "an HD companion is retargeting FROM this driver's bones this frame. A rider must not also write
  them (it would feed the companion a perturbed source pose) and the stock mesh is suppressed
  anyway, so the companion's own chains do the work."
  (let ((now (the int (current-time)))
        (slot -1))
    (dotimes (i 16)
      (when (and (< slot 0) (= (-> *phys-cover-pid* i) pid))
        (set! slot i)))
    (when (< slot 0)
      (dotimes (i 16)
        (when (and (< slot 0) (> (- now (-> *phys-cover-stamp* i)) 8))
          (set! slot i))))
    (when (>= slot 0)
      (set! (-> *phys-cover-pid* slot) pid)
      (set! (-> *phys-cover-stamp* slot) now)))
  (none))

(defun phys-covered? ((pid int))
  (let ((now (the int (current-time)))
        (r #f))
    (dotimes (i 16)
      (when (and (= (-> *phys-cover-pid* i) pid)
                 (<= (- now (-> *phys-cover-stamp* i)) 8))
        (set! r #t)))
    r))

(defun phys-rider-post! ((obj process-drawable))
  "post-anim chain sim for STOCK actors. Called from process-drawable::do-joint-math! for every
  drawable in the game, so the fast path out is the whole design: four pointer tests, one type
  compare and one enabled-check when the feature is off or the actor has no rig."
  (when (and (nonzero? (-> obj draw))
             (nonzero? (-> obj skel))
             (nonzero? (-> obj draw jgeo))
             (nonzero? (-> obj draw skeleton))
             (not (logtest? (-> obj draw status) (draw-status hidden no-anim)))
             (!= (-> obj type) jak-hd)
             (> (pc-physics-enabled) 0))
    ;; one window tick per frame, shared by every rider
    (let ((now (the int (current-time))))
      (when (!= now *phys-rider-last*)
        (set! *phys-rider-last* now)
        ;; The physics menu-row audit used to hang off the COMPANION spawn, so a session with
        ;; ENHANCED MODELS off never ran it — and that is precisely a session where the menu still
        ;; shows both physics rows. It is self-capping (*phys-menu-audited*), so calling it from the
        ;; rider tick as well simply makes the audit independent of whether HD models are on.
        (physics-menu-static-audit!)
        (+! *phys-rider-frames* 1)
        (when (>= *phys-rider-frames* 300)
          (format 0 "[HD-PHYS-RIDER] window: bound=~D active=~D slots-full=~D~%"
                  *phys-rider-bound* *phys-rider-active* *phys-rider-full*)
          (set! *phys-rider-frames* 0)
          (set! *phys-rider-active* 0)
          (set! *phys-rider-full* 0))))
    (let* ((pid (the int (-> obj pid)))
           (slot (phys-slot-find pid)))
      (cond
        ;; --- HD-OWNED ACTOR ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        ;; An actor an HD companion is (or is about to be) retargeting FROM must never be written by
        ;; a rider: the companion reads these very bones, so a chain-perturbed source pose would
        ;; shake the HD model too.
        ;; The first test is the load-bearing one, and it is STATELESS: same question the spawner
        ;; asks — "with enhanced models on, does this driver model have an HD replacement for the
        ;; current look?". The per-frame cover STAMP alone was not enough: measured on the village1
        ;; leg, Jak and Daxter re-bound 98 times each in 110 s because a companion's cover lapses
        ;; between despawn and respawn, and every one of those gaps let a rider grab the driver for
        ;; a while. With the stateless test the answer cannot flicker with process lifetime.
        ;; The stamp is kept as a second net for anything the name test cannot see.
        ((or (and (-> *pc-settings* recharged-enhanced-models?)
                  (nonzero? (-> obj draw mgeo))
                  (>= (hd-desired-entry-for-mgeo (-> obj draw mgeo name)) 0))
             (phys-covered? pid))
         (when (and (>= slot 0) (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot)))
           (phys-slot-free! slot)))
        ((>= slot 0)
         (when (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot))
           ;; ONCE PER FRAME. Several states call do-joint-math! more than once per frame
           ;; (logic-target has three call sites, ja-post has another); stepping twice would
           ;; double the sim's time step for those actors only.
           (let ((now (the int (current-time))))
             (when (!= now (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot))
               (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot) now)
               (+! *phys-rider-active* 1)
               (phys-slot-step! slot (-> obj draw) (-> obj draw jgeo name) (-> obj draw jgeo length))))))
        (else
         ;; is this RIG configured? One map lookup on a short string per unbound drawable per frame —
         ;; deliberately NOT cached on the jgeo pointer: a level unload can hand the same address to
         ;; a different rig, and a stale negative would silently un-physics a character.
         (let ((nch (pc-physics-num-chains (-> obj draw jgeo name)))
               (key (the int (-> obj draw jgeo)))
               (known 0))
           (dotimes (i *phys-seen-n*)
             (when (= (-> *phys-seen-jgeo* i) key)
               (set! known 1)))
           (when (and (zero? known) (< *phys-seen-n* PHYS-RIDER-SEEN))
             (set! (-> *phys-seen-jgeo* *phys-seen-n*) key)
             (+! *phys-seen-n* 1)
             (format 0 "[HD-PHYS-RIDER] rig ~S chains=~D~%" (-> obj draw jgeo name) nch))
         (when (> nch 0)
           (let ((s (phys-slot-claim pid 1)))
             (cond
               ((< s 0)
                (+! *phys-rider-full* 1))
               (else
                (phys-fill-par-from-jgeo! s (-> obj draw jgeo) (-> obj draw jgeo length))
                (phys-slot-bind! s (-> obj draw) (-> obj draw jgeo name) (-> obj draw jgeo length))
                (+! *phys-rider-bound* 1))))))))))
  (none))

) ;; #when FLAG_PHYSICS
